\begin{align*}
1 - \cos^2 x + 1 - \cos^2 2x + 1 - \cos^2 3x + 1 - \cos^2 4x &= 2 \\
4 - (\cos^2 x + \cos^2 2x + \cos^2 3x + \cos^2 4x) &= 2 \\
\cos^2 x + \cos^2 2x + \cos^2 3x + \cos^2 4x &= 2.
\end{align*}
From this, we can see that the original equation is actually $\cos^2 x + \cos^2 2x + \cos^2 3x + \cos^2 4x = 2$. We can further rewrite this equation as
\begin{align*}
(\cos 4x - \cos 2x)^2 - (\cos 4x + \cos 2x)^2 &= 0 \\
(\cos 3x + \cos x)^2 - (\cos 3x - \cos x)^2 &= 0 \\
(\cos 5x + \cos x)(\cos 5x - \cos x) = 0.
\end{align*}
